  },
  {
    "episode_id": 83468,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83468.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, I can't even speculate. I know that there is a desire on the part of the White House to sort of retool that so that it reflects their administration priorities and not a continuation of the Obama programs. And as it applies to this particular legislation, this we hope will be included as part of their policy because It really has nothing to do with anything that President Obama did or didn't do. It's mostly, this has been something that's been talked about for years and years. And as it stands right now by statute, US ag commodities can sell ag products in Cuba. The problem is they have to, it's required that they have cash up front.",
