    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, there are a number of things. One thing I thought, just everyday Cubans that you meet on the street and out in the, you know, we didn't, we left Havana and went out into the countryside and did some small villages and interacted with farmers and things of this nature. I went to a farmers market outside of Havana. And what I found was that there is, they're very welcoming of Americans, number one. And number two, they recognize the quality and the value proposition of having US ag products there because it's so close. And it's such good quality in comparison to some of the other products that they get that they would love to be able to of Elden cells of U.S. agricultural commodities. And I think just in general, the spirit of the Cuban people is very",
